{title: Trust and Obey}
{key: C}
{time: 3/4}
{columns:2}

{start_of_verse: 1}
When we [C]walk with the [**]Lord
In the [G]light of His [C]Word
What a [F]glory He [C]sheds on our [G]way
While we [C]do His good [**]will
He a[G]bides with us [C]still
And with [F]all who will [G]trust and o[C]bey
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G]Trust and o[C]bey! 
For there's [A]no other [Dm]way 
To be [G]happy in [C]Jesus
But to [G]trust and o[C]bey
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
Not a [C]burden we [**]bear
Not a [G]sorrow we [C]share
But our [F]toil He doth [C]richly re[G]pay
Not a [C]grief or a [**]loss
Not a [G]frown or a [C]cross
But is [F]blest if we [G]trust and o[C]bey
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: 3}
But we [C]never can [**]prove
The de[G]lights of His [C]love
Until [F]all on the [C]altar we [G]lay
For the [C]favor He [**]shows
And the [G]joy He be[C]stows
Are for [F]them who will [G]trust and o[C]bey
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: 4}
Then in [C]fellowship [**]sweet
We will [G]sit at His [C]feet
Or we'll [F]walk by His [C]side in the [G]way
What He [C]says we will [**]do
Where He [G]sends we will [C]go
Never [F]fear, only [G]trust and o[C]bey
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
